WEBVTT

00:00.959 --> 00:04.379
In the year 845, the Colossal Titan

00:04.629 --> 00:08.133
and the Armored Titan suddenly appeared.

00:08.341 --> 00:11.678
They destroyed one of humanity's walls,
and with it, everyday life.

00:12.679 --> 00:17.267
And then, finally freed
from their century-long hunger,

00:17.600 --> 00:20.020
the Titans overran humankind once again.

00:20.103 --> 00:23.773
Stop!

00:23.982 --> 00:26.443
Humanity abandoned Wall Maria,

00:27.152 --> 00:30.530
lost twenty percent of its population
and a third of its territory,

00:30.989 --> 00:34.617
and was forced to retreat
behind Wall Rose.

02:16.427 --> 02:18.138
YEAR 850

02:19.848 --> 02:21.391
2 YEARS AFTER JOINING THE CORPS

02:21.474 --> 02:24.269
Pick up the pace!
Run, you lead-footed laggards!

02:26.146 --> 02:27.564
What's your problem, Arlelt?

02:28.148 --> 02:29.399
You're dragging your feet!

02:30.817 --> 02:34.612
Too heavy for you? Maybe you'd prefer
I let you drop your gear?

02:36.156 --> 02:39.617
If this was a real mission,
you'd be Titan food by now!

02:41.911 --> 02:42.829
Damn...

02:43.872 --> 02:44.789
Give it to me!

02:46.249 --> 02:50.587
You're going to fail at this rate!
We're being graded today!

02:51.170 --> 02:54.215
But you'll get points
marked off too if you do that...

02:54.299 --> 02:58.094
Then make the grade without getting
found out before I change my mind!

03:01.431 --> 03:02.849
Reiner Braun.

03:04.893 --> 03:07.896
Dedicated in both mind and body,

03:07.979 --> 03:10.315
and well respected by his comrades.

03:13.026 --> 03:15.570
I refuse to be a burden,
even if it costs me my life!

03:21.034 --> 03:22.702
Armin Arlelt.

03:22.869 --> 03:24.621
Though physically frail,

03:24.704 --> 03:26.998
his aptitude in the classroom
is extraordinary.

03:44.682 --> 03:46.059
Annie Leonhart.

03:46.434 --> 03:48.519
Her slice attacks are absolutely flawless,

03:48.645 --> 03:51.356
but her reclusive nature makes her
a poor fit for team missions.

03:51.731 --> 03:53.191
Bertholdt Hoover.

03:53.483 --> 03:56.986
He possesses remarkable potential,
but lacks aggression.

03:57.862 --> 03:59.072
Jean Kirschtein.

03:59.572 --> 04:01.449
Top-class omnidirectional mobility.

04:01.574 --> 04:05.161
But his volatile personality tends
to cause friction with others.

04:07.538 --> 04:09.457
I can't slice as good as those two!

04:10.041 --> 04:12.085
I'll just have to find
the Titans before them!

04:14.921 --> 04:16.798
If anyone is going to
get into the Military Police...

04:17.173 --> 04:18.174
it's going to be me!

04:21.636 --> 04:23.137
Thanks for your help, Jean!

04:24.514 --> 04:26.766
Following you was a good idea!

04:30.103 --> 04:32.188
Oh, yes!

04:33.606 --> 04:34.899
Sasha Braus.

04:35.275 --> 04:37.277
She has unconventionally good intuition,

04:37.360 --> 04:39.862
but also demonstrates
poor teamwork as a result.

04:41.030 --> 04:42.323
Conny Springer.

04:42.615 --> 04:47.412
He excels at executing quick turns,
but is also a bit dim-witted.

04:47.745 --> 04:48.621
Here they come.

04:57.338 --> 04:59.549
Damn! It's not as deep as Mikasa's again!

05:00.341 --> 05:01.926
Mikasa Ackermann.

05:02.260 --> 05:04.345
Completely proficient in every area.

05:04.679 --> 05:07.849
It's suitable to say she's an unmatched,
unprecedented talent.

05:08.808 --> 05:10.101
Eren Jaeger.

05:10.351 --> 05:12.729
No real specialties,
but he has improved his grades

05:12.812 --> 05:14.605
with his unparalleled effort.

05:15.315 --> 05:19.277
And he possesses twice
the sense of purpose than anyone else.

05:35.626 --> 05:37.128
That hurt!

05:38.129 --> 05:40.882
Sorry. I'm bad at knowing
how much force to apply.

05:42.759 --> 05:45.303
Now it's your turn to be the rogue.

05:47.013 --> 05:47.889
What's the matter?

05:48.806 --> 05:50.683
I don't get this training.

05:52.018 --> 05:54.312
Why would soldiers fight other people?

05:55.104 --> 05:58.608
Only an idiot would take on
a target barehanded.

06:01.194 --> 06:03.029
That's irresponsible thinking.

06:04.155 --> 06:05.656
We're soldiers.

06:06.115 --> 06:09.827
There are times when we can't run away,
no matter how bad the situation is.

06:10.369 --> 06:13.247
No matter what the enemy is,
we have to be ready for it,

06:13.331 --> 06:15.208
whether it means cannons
or hand-to-hand combat.

06:16.959 --> 06:20.630
I believe that's the responsibility
of a strong soldier.

06:22.423 --> 06:24.258
Anyway, look over there.

06:26.260 --> 06:28.221
Oh, that's Annie.

06:29.222 --> 06:31.974
She's slacking off
without the commandant noticing again.

06:32.350 --> 06:36.020
All right, Eren.
That slouch needs to learn a lesson.

06:36.312 --> 06:40.274
Let's teach her
how a soldier is supposed to act.

06:40.608 --> 06:41.567
What?

06:45.404 --> 06:47.615
Not fond of the commandant's headbutts?

06:47.949 --> 06:50.159
If you don't want to end up any shorter,

06:50.493 --> 06:53.496
think back to when you first came
and start taking things seriously.

06:53.830 --> 06:55.790
Hey, why are you being so rude?

06:59.043 --> 07:00.628
Man, she's mad.

07:00.962 --> 07:03.256
I thought she looked
scary enough as it is,

07:03.548 --> 07:06.050
but that's nothing
compared to when she's pissed.

07:06.300 --> 07:08.177
All right! Get started, Eren!

07:08.261 --> 07:09.512
Me?

07:15.810 --> 07:18.020
You know how to do this, right, Annie?

07:18.271 --> 07:19.355
Here I come!

07:23.776 --> 07:25.611
What the...

07:25.987 --> 07:27.405
She kicked my leg?

07:28.823 --> 07:30.408
Can I go now?

07:30.491 --> 07:33.453
No! The drill's not over
until you take the dagger!

07:35.288 --> 07:36.456
Wait, Annie!

07:36.539 --> 07:38.541
You're supposed to do this a certain way!

07:46.591 --> 07:47.508
There.

07:48.885 --> 07:51.387
Now it's your turn to attack me.

07:52.138 --> 07:53.764
No... I'm not...

07:53.973 --> 07:55.516
Do it, Reiner.

07:56.267 --> 07:59.645
I thought you wanted to teach her
about a soldier's responsibility?

08:03.524 --> 08:07.153
Yes, sometimes a soldier can't back down.

08:08.446 --> 08:09.947
This is one of those times!

08:15.286 --> 08:17.079
That's an amazing technique.

08:17.288 --> 08:18.956
Who did you learn it from?

08:19.624 --> 08:20.875
My father.

08:21.209 --> 08:24.045
- Your dad came up with that move?
- Why does it matter?

08:24.879 --> 08:27.507
There's no point in any of this.

08:28.132 --> 08:29.717
You mean this training?

08:30.801 --> 08:33.721
We aren't graded on
our hand-to-hand combat skills.

08:34.096 --> 08:36.349
Most people brush it off, like them.

08:37.141 --> 08:40.770
Because only the top ten cadets are
allowed to join the Military Police

08:40.978 --> 08:43.189
and serve in the interior.

08:43.898 --> 08:47.902
The only ones who take it seriously
are naive idiots like you...

08:48.444 --> 08:49.987
or just ordinary idiots.

08:51.239 --> 08:52.615
Crap! The commandant!

08:55.326 --> 08:59.872
For some reason, in this world,
the better you are at fighting Titans,

08:59.956 --> 09:01.749
the further you can get away from them.

09:02.500 --> 09:04.752
How do you think this farce came about?

09:05.294 --> 09:07.630
I don't know... That's a good question!

09:12.218 --> 09:15.805
Maybe because it's human nature?

09:22.728 --> 09:26.065
Anyway, I refuse to be stupid enough

09:26.148 --> 09:30.152
to play soldiers in this stupid world.

09:33.406 --> 09:35.992
Looks like you're
not much of a warrior at all.

09:38.494 --> 09:41.330
I was so caught up in getting stronger
that I never realized it.

09:41.831 --> 09:43.749
It's such a clear contradiction...

09:44.834 --> 09:47.753
They're honing their Titan-killing skills

09:47.837 --> 09:50.047
just to get away from the Titans!

09:55.344 --> 09:56.762
It can't be helped.

09:57.221 --> 10:01.559
Before Wall Maria fell, only the Scouts
needed omnidirectional mobility.

10:01.642 --> 10:03.477
And they're a small regiment

10:03.978 --> 10:06.397
- that put ODM expertise at risk...
- Do quick, strong blasts.

10:06.480 --> 10:10.651
- So this was a way to prevent...
- Relying on inertia will save you gas.

10:11.360 --> 10:12.945
Easier said than done.

10:13.154 --> 10:16.824
Yes, maybe not everyone can pull it off...

10:18.409 --> 10:20.494
But there's no harm in knowing

10:20.578 --> 10:22.705
if you want to join the Military Police.

10:22.788 --> 10:25.291
Yes! I'd love to get in!

10:25.583 --> 10:29.378
Working near the king...
There's no greater honor than that!

10:29.754 --> 10:30.880
Hold on, Marco!

10:32.506 --> 10:35.301
Quit talking like a goody two-shoes
and say what you really think!

10:35.509 --> 10:37.178
You want to join the Military Police

10:37.261 --> 10:41.015
because it means having a safe,
comfy life in the interior!

10:41.098 --> 10:42.975
No! I really do want to--

10:43.100 --> 10:44.727
It's comfy in the interior?

10:46.228 --> 10:49.565
Five years ago,
this used to be the interior too.

10:50.316 --> 10:52.902
What's your point, Eren?

10:54.320 --> 10:56.989
Jean, you don't need
to go to the interior.

10:57.657 --> 11:00.284
I'd say your head is nice
and spacious enough as it is.

11:03.412 --> 11:04.497
You little...

11:04.580 --> 11:08.584
Honing your Titan-killing skills
just to get away from the Titans...

11:08.668 --> 11:11.629
Doesn't that seem
like a weird system to you?

11:11.962 --> 11:13.339
You only say that now?

11:13.756 --> 11:16.926
I want that stupid system
to stay in place, for my sake.

11:17.426 --> 11:18.677
You piece of scum!

11:18.761 --> 11:20.554
Shut up! This is the real world!

11:20.638 --> 11:22.139
Eren! Quit it!

11:22.223 --> 11:23.432
Stop that.

11:28.396 --> 11:30.356
- Screw you!
- What?

11:30.439 --> 11:31.941
Let go! You're going to rip it!

11:32.024 --> 11:34.110
I don't give a damn
about your clothes! I'm jealous!

11:34.193 --> 11:35.611
What are you talking about?

11:43.786 --> 11:44.620
I see it now.

11:44.870 --> 11:49.333
He always has to
take his feelings out on others.

11:49.792 --> 11:51.293
Just like I always do.

11:52.169 --> 11:53.712
But not this time!

11:56.340 --> 11:59.218
I'm going to use that move
to take control of the situation!

12:09.895 --> 12:11.730
What the hell was that?

12:12.022 --> 12:16.235
A combat technique I learned the hard way
while you were screwing around.

12:18.571 --> 12:21.824
A carefree, capricious life
is your idea of the real world?

12:22.491 --> 12:26.245
And you honestly call yourself a soldier?

12:35.045 --> 12:37.965
I heard a loud noise just now.

12:38.466 --> 12:41.051
Would anyone care to explain?

12:47.183 --> 12:48.642
It was Sasha. She farted.

12:48.726 --> 12:49.560
What?

12:49.643 --> 12:51.437
You again?

12:53.314 --> 12:55.191
Learn some decency, will you?

13:04.742 --> 13:09.747
The 218 cadets went on
to reach graduation.

13:12.750 --> 13:14.084
Give your hearts!

13:14.460 --> 13:15.544
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

13:16.212 --> 13:21.759
You have three options
after you graduate from the Cadets today!

13:22.259 --> 13:26.138
The Garrison Regiment, which reinforces
the walls and protects each city!

13:26.472 --> 13:28.098
The Scout Regiment,

13:28.182 --> 13:30.851
which risks life and limb to venture
into Titan territory outside the walls!

13:30.935 --> 13:33.854
And the Military Police Regiment,
which serves under the king

13:33.938 --> 13:35.689
by policing the people
and preserving order!

13:36.065 --> 13:38.901
Of course, the only ones
allowed to join the Military Police

13:39.235 --> 13:42.238
are the aforementioned top ten cadets!

13:48.911 --> 13:51.080
We've finally made it here...

13:52.164 --> 13:53.791
Now it's our turn

13:54.583 --> 13:56.544
to devour the Titans!

14:01.340 --> 14:02.299
I did it!

14:02.383 --> 14:04.009
I'm in the Military Police!

14:04.093 --> 14:06.136
No more worrying about food!

14:07.346 --> 14:09.807
How did I get ranked under Eren?

14:10.099 --> 14:11.100
Damn!

14:12.017 --> 14:14.937
Are you seriously not joining
the Military Police Regiment, Eren?

14:15.062 --> 14:17.606
Even after you got
into the top ten and all?

14:18.107 --> 14:19.942
My mind was set from the very start.

14:20.609 --> 14:24.029
I didn't train all this time
to live in the interior.

14:24.530 --> 14:26.240
I did it to fight the Titans.

14:26.824 --> 14:28.033
We can't beat them!

14:32.413 --> 14:36.417
You know how many
people have been eaten so far...

14:36.792 --> 14:40.004
The answer was clear after we lost
20 percent of our population.

14:41.297 --> 14:44.758
Humanity can't beat the Titans.

14:50.931 --> 14:51.932
So?

14:53.934 --> 14:55.978
You're going to give up
because you don't think we can win?

14:57.438 --> 15:01.066
- Well...
- Yes, humanity has been losing so far.

15:01.692 --> 15:03.986
But that's because we were
clueless about the Titans!

15:05.029 --> 15:07.615
Material warfare is useless against them.

15:08.115 --> 15:12.786
We lost, but the information we gained
in battle will lead to our hope!

15:13.704 --> 15:16.749
Are we just going to throw away
all the advances in techniques

15:16.832 --> 15:20.127
that cost us thousands of lives
so we can be the Titans' food?

15:20.711 --> 15:21.837
To hell with that!

15:22.713 --> 15:26.342
I'm going to drive out every last Titan

15:26.425 --> 15:28.135
and leave these cramped walls!

15:28.761 --> 15:30.179
That's my dream!

15:30.804 --> 15:34.391
Humanity hasn't truly been defeated yet!

15:42.274 --> 15:43.609
Wait, Eren!

15:44.860 --> 15:47.905
If you want to go outside the walls,
be my guest!

15:48.489 --> 15:50.950
I'm going to join the Military Police!

16:01.126 --> 16:04.380
Eren. That stuff about
your dream earlier...

16:04.463 --> 16:06.799
Yes, I borrowed those ideas of yours

16:07.049 --> 16:09.218
about going outside
instead of staying inside.

16:11.804 --> 16:13.847
I'm going to join the Scout Regiment!

16:14.932 --> 16:16.433
Are you serious, Armin?

16:16.684 --> 16:19.645
You were the top in classroom studies!
You should put that to use!

16:20.020 --> 16:22.564
I won't be a burden,
even if it costs me my life.

16:23.774 --> 16:25.526
I'll join the Scouts too.

16:26.193 --> 16:29.613
Hey! You graduated top of the class!
You should join the Military Police!

16:30.197 --> 16:34.368
If you join the Military Police,
then I will too.

16:35.244 --> 16:39.248
If you join the Garrison Regiment,
then I will too.

16:39.957 --> 16:43.669
Because you'll die early
unless I'm around.

16:44.878 --> 16:46.964
I never asked for your help.

16:47.881 --> 16:50.718
I don't want to lose
any more of my family.

17:13.615 --> 17:16.243
It's here! The main unit
of the Scout Regiment!

17:17.036 --> 17:20.164
Commander Erwin,
give those Titans a real thrashing!

17:21.582 --> 17:23.417
Look! It's Captain Levi!

17:24.877 --> 17:27.504
They say he's as mighty
as an entire brigade!

17:28.672 --> 17:30.007
Talk about annoying...

17:30.424 --> 17:32.342
This is nothing like five years ago!

17:32.551 --> 17:35.554
People actually feel hopeful
about the Scout members!

17:36.096 --> 17:38.474
Yes, everyone has cheered up since then.

17:38.932 --> 17:40.642
Nothing has happened in five years.

17:41.310 --> 17:43.395
They've upgraded the mounted cannons too.

17:43.771 --> 17:45.981
I doubt the Colossal Titan will show up.

17:46.148 --> 17:47.066
Yes!

17:47.691 --> 17:49.985
That's a load of crap, you idiotic couple!

17:50.194 --> 17:52.696
What? Us, a married couple?

17:52.905 --> 17:54.448
You're getting ahead of yourself, Eren!

17:55.866 --> 17:57.201
Hey, guys!

17:58.285 --> 17:59.453
Mr. Hannes!

18:00.621 --> 18:03.165
I heard you graduated yesterday.

18:03.582 --> 18:05.834
Man, you brats have really grown up.

18:06.168 --> 18:07.544
You too, Mr. Hannes!

18:07.628 --> 18:10.214
You used to be a drunkard, but now
you're the chief of Corps of Engineers.

18:10.297 --> 18:11.465
Oh, you!

18:13.759 --> 18:17.805
I'm sorry I couldn't save your mom.

18:20.015 --> 18:21.433
It wasn't your fault.

18:23.102 --> 18:24.645
We're not ignorant anymore.

18:25.562 --> 18:27.773
We won't let another
tragedy like that happen.

18:29.441 --> 18:30.943
We will defeat the Titans!

18:35.739 --> 18:38.659
I don't know if I should be happy
that you've grown up or not.

18:40.202 --> 18:41.370
Don't go dying, now.

18:43.872 --> 18:44.706
What?

18:45.124 --> 18:46.959
You're joining the Scouts?

18:47.209 --> 18:50.087
Conny! You were so set
on the Military Police!

18:50.170 --> 18:52.339
Yes, I was! But...

18:52.923 --> 18:55.801
Sounds like your speech
yesterday won him over!

18:55.968 --> 18:56.802
What?

18:57.094 --> 18:58.178
Mind your own business!

18:58.512 --> 19:00.722
I decided on my own!

19:01.390 --> 19:02.891
Don't be so embarrassed.

19:04.059 --> 19:05.269
You're not the only one.

19:07.437 --> 19:08.480
Thomas...

19:08.730 --> 19:09.648
You don't mean...

19:10.065 --> 19:11.733
Well, everyone?

19:12.818 --> 19:15.988
I brought some meat
from the officers' storehouse!

19:17.531 --> 19:20.159
Sasha! Do you want to end up
in solitary confinement?

19:20.242 --> 19:21.827
You really are crazy!

19:21.910 --> 19:23.245
So much that it's scary...

19:23.579 --> 19:25.956
We can all share it later...

19:26.123 --> 19:28.417
All sliced up and between some bread...

19:29.543 --> 19:31.503
- Go put it back!
- Yes!

19:31.837 --> 19:35.048
After we lost all that land,
meat has become really valuable.

19:35.424 --> 19:36.717
It'll be fine!

19:40.971 --> 19:44.808
We can just get more cattle and sheep
once we retake our land!

19:50.105 --> 19:51.565
I'll have some meat too!

19:51.940 --> 19:54.359
Me too! Save me some!

19:55.402 --> 19:57.321
I'll have some too, of course!

19:57.779 --> 19:58.989
Guys...

19:59.740 --> 20:01.283
Why are you just standing there, Eren?

20:01.825 --> 20:04.328
We'll get caught
if we don't get back to work!

20:04.703 --> 20:06.288
Lunch will take a while!

20:13.128 --> 20:14.713
Five years have passed since then...

20:16.173 --> 20:19.593
Humanity is finally regaining its dignity.

20:21.511 --> 20:22.512
We can win!

20:25.098 --> 20:26.725
Humanity's counterattack...

20:28.435 --> 20:29.561
is just beginning!

20:50.749 --> 20:51.792
That's hot!

20:51.875 --> 20:53.001
What the...

21:00.217 --> 21:01.468
Samuel!

21:02.552 --> 21:03.595
Sasha!

21:12.104 --> 21:13.146
Samuel!

21:13.230 --> 21:14.648
Stay still!

21:15.899 --> 21:16.984
That was close!

21:20.112 --> 21:21.363
The wall...

21:21.613 --> 21:22.990
It's broken!

21:24.283 --> 21:26.535
It's happening again!

21:26.785 --> 21:28.537
The Titans are going to get in!

21:31.832 --> 21:33.458
I'm going to drive out...

21:34.376 --> 21:36.378
every last one of them from this world!

21:38.171 --> 21:40.841
Every... last one...

21:43.510 --> 21:45.304
Mounted Artillery Maintenance Squad Four!

21:45.387 --> 21:47.055
Prepare for battle!

21:48.265 --> 21:50.976
The target is
the Colossal Titan dead ahead!

21:51.143 --> 21:53.979
This is our chance! Don't let it get away!

22:03.947 --> 22:05.324
Hey there.

22:06.783 --> 22:08.452
It has been five years, hasn't it?

23:44.506 --> 23:46.883
Hell opens its mouth once more.

23:47.884 --> 23:51.596
The Titans devour the soldiers
before they can even catch their breaths.

23:52.514 --> 23:57.185
Amidst this, Eren saves Armin
from the brink of death, but...
